The branching fraction for the decay $B^{0} \to D_{s}^{-} K^{+}$ was determined using an independent sample of $B^{0} \to D^{-} \pi^{+}$ mesons, which served as a reference. The $D_{s}^{-} K^{+}$ candidates were identified by analyzing the decay chain $D_{s}^{-} \to \pi^{-} \bar{D}^{0} \to \pi^{-} \pi^{-} \mu^{+} \nu_{\mu}$, while the $D^{-} \pi^{+}$ candidates were reconstructed via the $D^{-} \to \bar{D}^{0} \pi^{-}$ mode with $D^{0} \to K^{+} \pi^{-}$ decays. The resulting branching fraction ratio is measured as:
$$ \frac{\mathcal{B}(B^{0} \to D_{s}^{-} K^{+})}{\mathcal{B}(B^{0} \to D^{-} \pi^{+})} = 0.90^{+0.18}_{-0.17} \pm 0.03 $$
